      "content": "It's truly heartbreaking to lose a significant part of yourself, but it's not uncommon to feel this way during profound changes in life. While the person you miss is physically gone, their essence and impact on you linger in meaningful ways. It may help to find ways to honor their memory while embracing the growth and change in your life. You don't have to carry their name alone; you can carry their teachings and lessons into new experiences that feel authentic to you. Finding a support system to share your feelings with can also be incredibly comforting during such times. It's okay to grieve, but also remember, you are more alive and capable than you realize.",
